    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p39-q13-stem",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Moses finds that for a Froghead eel, its mass is directly proportional to the square of its length.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p39-q13-given",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An eel of this species has a length of 72 cm and a mass of 8250 grams.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p39-q13-request",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What is the expected length of a Froghead eel with a mass of 10.2 kg?",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Give your answer to one decimal place.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$80.1\\text{ cm}$",
      "worked": "Let $m$ be mass in grams and $l$ be length in centimetres.\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=kl^2\\\\8250&=k(72)^2\\\\k&=\\frac{8250}{72^2}\\\\10.2\\text{ kg}&=10200\\text{ g}\\\\10200&=\\frac{8250}{72^2}l^2\\\\l&=\\sqrt{\\frac{10200\\times72^2}{8250}}\\\\l&\\approx80.1\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\nUse the positive square root because length is positive.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
  },
